## Interface: 30300
## Title: Diablocraft
## Notes: Diablocraft screens with no stock WoW equivalent.
## Author: Diablocraft
## Version: 0.1
## Dependencies: AIO_Client
## X-Torment-Client-Patch: 86
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: DiablocraftUI

# Lua first: the XML's OnLoad handlers call into the table it defines.
# Strings.lua sets the tooltip unit globals before any tooltip is drawn.
Strings.lua
# ResourceNames.lua is generated by generate_class_resources.py; ResourceText.lua
# reads it to put each class's D3 resource word in place of the slot's WoW word
# (docs/contracts/resource-names.md). Generated first.
ResourceNames.lua
# PowerStrings.lua gives each class power token its PowerBarColor entry, name and
# cost formats (docs/contracts/class-powers.md); before ResourceText.lua, which
# reads the PowerBarColor keys at load.
PowerStrings.lua
ResourceText.lua
# TooltipBorder.lua colours an item tooltip's border from the name colour dc_tooltip.lua draws.
TooltipBorder.lua
# Version.lua reports X-Torment-Client-Patch to the AIO handshake; one notice.
Version.lua
# Economy.lua defines Diablocraft.Econ, which Stash.lua's stash draws from.
Economy.lua
# LifeText.lua writes the stock unit frames' Life text from UnitHealth with Economy.lua's formatter.
LifeText.lua
# The core, in this order: ArtSlots.lua makes the Diablocraft table and DC.SetArt; PanelKit.lua is
# the border kit; WindowStyle.lua is DC.Style; Stash.lua is the stash screen and its AIO bridge, and
# reads what the three before it publish on the table.
ArtSlots.lua
PanelKit.lua
WindowStyle.lua
Stash.lua
Stash.xml
# Inventory.lua defines the handlers Inventory.xml's OnLoad calls, and its
# frames use DiablocraftButtonTemplate, which Stash.xml declares - so both come
# first, in that order.
Inventory.lua
Inventory.xml

# The channelled skills (spell id -> skill) and the observer of the stock action buttons, ElvUI's
# bars and the bound keys that starts and stops them (hold-to-channel); the list loads first.
ChannelSpells.lua
ChannelObserver.lua

# The one strip the on-screen buttons share: the bug button (below).
# Needs the Diablocraft table, made by ArtSlots.lua above.
ButtonStrip.lua

# The Dungeon Finder probe: LFGRows.lua is generated by
# generate_lfg_dungeons.py (visible row -> hidden row); LFG.lua reads it.
LFGRows.lua
LFG.lua

# The /bug window and its on-screen button; needs DC.Style (WindowStyle.lua) and
# DC.SetArt (ArtSlots.lua), loaded above.
BugReport.lua

# The pylon and shrine minimap pins: the DCPYLON reader and the pins.
# MapBounds.lua is generated by client-patch/build_map_bounds.py (the client's WorldMapArea.dbc
# as Lua, with the rift_open_zones rectangles for the bounty panel); Pylons.lua reads it.
MapBounds.lua
Pylons.lua

# The bounty board on the stock world map: the DCBOUNTY reader, the 5x5
# panel and the zone waypoint markers. Needs ArtSlots.lua (DC.SetArt), WindowStyle.lua (DC.Style) and
# MapBounds.lua (Diablocraft.MapBounds, Diablocraft.MapZones), loaded above.
BountyMap.lua

# The rifts' centre-screen lines: the DCRIFTTEXT reader and the fading text (docs/contracts/rift-centre-text.md).
# Needs only the Diablocraft table, which it makes itself.
RiftText.lua

# The stock Shaman totem bar (MultiCastActionBarFrame) hidden at login; needs only the stock frame.
StockTotemBar.lua
